From bb1c103f69b1b03f8042108abcc89d85e9e71ac2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:43:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 58/70] demux: flac: leave the stream on the frame the seek
 found

RefineSeek finds the wanted frame by feeding the stream to the
packetizer until a frame comes out, and the packetizer only closes a
frame once it has seen the head of the one after it, so by the time the
search is happy the stream sits one or two frames beyond the target. The
next Demux() then hands out that later frame and everything in between
is simply never played. At 4096 samples a frame and 44.1 kHz that is
186 ms lost from every seek, and from the head of every pass when the
input repeats an item by seeking back to the start.

Put the stream back where the iteration that matched began reading. The
frame is parsed again, which costs nothing next to what it buys, and the
preroll the caller set with ES_OUT_SET_NEXT_DISPLAY_TIME is what drops
whatever precedes the wanted time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/flac.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/flac.c b/modules/demux/flac.c
index 81129cb5fb..8f006999a7 100644
--- a/modules/demux/flac.c
+++ b/modules/demux/flac.c
@@ -349,6 +349,14 @@ static int RefineSeek( demux_t *p_demux, vlc_tick_t i_time, double i_bytemicrora
         }
     }
 
+    /* The search consumed the frame it was after, and the packetizer needed
+     * the head of the one behind it to close it, so the stream is left a frame
+     * or two past the target. Put it back where the iteration that matched
+     * started reading: the next Demux() then delivers the frame the seek asked
+     * for instead of one the caller never gets to hear. */
+    if( b_found && vlc_stream_Seek( p_demux->s, i_start_pos ) != VLC_SUCCESS )
+        return VLC_EGENERIC;
+
     return b_found ? VLC_SUCCESS : VLC_EGENERIC;
 }
 
